+## Launch continuation implementation
+
+Normal Finder launch had no --review-window argument, so the old delegate only created a menu icon. UI3 now uses one BatonMainWindowController from the executable delegate for ordinary launch, reopen and menu-bar actions. Removing the separate SwiftUI Window scene avoids divergent routing; native style contains titled, closable, miniaturizable, resizable with fullScreenPrimary, preserving AppKit’s fullscreen state. The controller retains the host/model on close and deminiaturizes when shown again; closing the window keeps the menu app running. Regular activation provides normal Dock/window behavior, as Ibrahim requested.
